From d96b21320ea0ab3c5af3e0a705ea96d9fa21205b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tao Liu <ltao@redhat.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 16:53:18 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] [PATCH 3/6] Prevent a multiply overflow in cache_init()

In cache_init(), malloc() takes the multiplication of info->page_size
and CACHE_SIZE. Since info->page_size is obtained from vmcoreinfo, a
malformed vmcore may contain a sufficiently large value to cause the
multiplication to overflow and wrap around to a small value. This can
later lead to an out-of-bounds access.

To mitigate the issue, let's check the value of page_size before set.

Signed-off-by: Tao Liu <ltao@redhat.com>
---
 makedumpfile.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/makedumpfile.c b/makedumpfile.c
index 810f667..b247587 100644
--- a/makedumpfile.c
+++ b/makedumpfile.c
@@ -1207,8 +1207,10 @@ is_page_size(long page_size)
 {
 	/*
 	 * Page size is restricted to a hamming weight of 1.
+	 * Limit page size within 1MB.
 	 */
-	if (page_size > 0 && !(page_size & (page_size - 1)))
+	if (page_size > 0 && !(page_size & (page_size - 1)) &&
+	    page_size <= (1 << 20))
 		return TRUE;
 
 	return FALSE;
